  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-01-01T16:23:50.671Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "At the moment, the Distance / Count hiding feature is a bit of a mixed bag with worlds that do performances.\n\nIn such worlds, the Stage usually is much further away than surrounding people / audience, leading to Actors / Performers to be hidden, while wasting the slots for people in the audience.\n\nI propose to add a feature to the SDK that allows to define priority loading zones.\n\nThese zones will, even if out of distance range, always show the avatars of people within that zone.\n\nThese avatars can be counted towards the total to show past the zone, but it should ensure that all avatars in that zone are shown first.\n\nOnly once people from this area are shown, should the normal closest to you routine take over and fill your count up till your set max.\n\nThis is a feature that would massively help with any kind of stage world.\n\nWeather it's using it on a DJ Booth in a club, or making a stage a priority zone to make sure people can always see actors.",
